(function(){var d={"book": {"chapters": [{"container": "EXTENSION", "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "kind": "ttrpg", "name": "Vampire: The Masquerade - Winter’s Teeth Vol. 1", "page": 1, "roots": ["#vA4kYnDgmhXwivshs9mwasY", "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM", "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV", "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ", "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "#vJIkg6w35VyWEHPFjBYdgJM", "#v2E5q9bGjiEZhACsWfskMvQ", "#vXolunYOWd2LBxkaeQiwz0W", "#vKkzz0XXNgApYgq7TNf7A65", "#vYXxWahyNkObxzS0XivMeFh", "#vujvJ8ZOHj2jiE6khpo8N8M"]}], "entities": ["#vA4kYnDgmhXwivshs9mwasY", "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM", "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV", "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ", "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "#vJIkg6w35VyWEHPFjBYdgJM", "#v2E5q9bGjiEZhACsWfskMvQ", "#vXolunYOWd2LBxkaeQiwz0W", "#vKkzz0XXNgApYgq7TNf7A65", "#vYXxWahyNkObxzS0XivMeFh", "#vujvJ8ZOHj2jiE6khpo8N8M"], "id": "winters-teeth", "kind": "book", "label": "Winter’s Teeth Vol. 1"}, "entities": {"#v1Bw5DQwhR49MbWP1oLpmXb": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#v90Lip3e5GbLG5sgyywEpEE"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v1Bw5DQwhR49MbWP1oLpmXb", "key": "Level 2", "name": "Level 2", "parent": "#vBcxuCG6uZOu9dlmYkiUjsQ", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v1QzV9xOVZp0nkqdKhWqalS": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Elena Kowalska was the daughter of an affluent Polish-Lithuanian family within Prague. As was often the custom with the daughters of the aristocracy, Elena was educated within a nunnery from the age of nine. By the time the young lady became a debutante at age eighteen, her family had already betrothed her to a kind and promising suitor.\n\nElena would never make her grand re-entry into high society, however, nor would she ever even lay eyes upon her groom-to-be. For none within the convent knew that their greatest patron, a wealthy Prussian widow by the name of Countess Gretel von Flemming, had taken a great interest in the youthful Elena, and took her under her wing to complete her true education.\n\nUnder the tutelage of Countess von Flemming, Elena learned that everything she had been taught of piety and prudence were simply pre-cursors. “One must first learn the rules of polite society,” Gretel had said, “before they can be broken for our benefit.\" Gretel trained Elena in how to navigate the world of nobility where her sex would not be viewed as a hindrance, but instead as her greatest weapon. For decades, the duo traveled the courts of Europe, and as Elena grew older and wiser, she had become molded into the Countess’ own image. Elena became the Countess’ prized pupil, and later, all but an equal in partnership. It was then that she was also schooled upon the secrets of everlasting life.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v1QzV9xOVZp0nkqdKhWqalS", "key": "Mortal Days:", "name": "Mortal Days:", "parent": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v1gEFg4SumJu8AfNJ7kBHgu": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Colleen Pendergrass (née Halstead) was born in 1976, the fourth of six children in a lower middle-class family.\n\nAt eighteen, Colleen had met Mitch Pendergrass, a high school dropout who had started working for her father’s HVAC company as a technician. Though four years older than her, Mitch and Colleen formulated a mutual attraction to one another, much to her father’s frustration. After two years of dating, Mitch and Colleen were married and, using the money saved from working at her father’s company, moved to Duluth and bought their first home.\n\nMitch found work at a towing company while Colleen set out to complete her RN training at community college, yet it seemed that every attempt at progress was met with setback after setback. Colleen eventually dropped out of college after becoming pregnant with her first child, Kady. Their son, Luke, would be born shortly after.\n\nMoney, stress and wasted opportunity all began to take their toll on the young couple, and as frustrations gave way to resentment, Mitch and Colleen’s relationship soon became perilously rocky.\n\nOne night, after venturing on a late-night call, Mitch disappeared. With Mitch missing, Colleen was suddenly filled with intense regret over the negativity with which she’d viewed her husband these past several months, and had promised herself to try and make it work, if only her spouse would return to her.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v1gEFg4SumJu8AfNJ7kBHgu", "key": "Mortal Days:", "name": "Mortal Days:", "parent": "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v1jnNoiN4y0AOCH8hKRjNW9": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Two nights after vanishing without a trace, Mitch returned just as mysteriously and suddenly as he had gone. Pale, cold and dirty, Colleen ushered her husband back into their home, when suddenly, he lunged upon her, sinking his teeth into her throat and draining the blood from her body. When Colleen awoke, she found herself lying in her bed, with Mitch’s lifeless corpse lying next to her. Confused, and possessed of a consuming hunger, Colleen got out of bed and pulled the blankets serving as makeshift curtains from the bedroom windows. As daylight poured in from the outside, Mitch’s corpse suddenly burst into flames – Colleen, herself, remained unburned. Acting on pure instinct, her emergency training kicked in and she covered the burning body with the heavy comforter, dousing the flames as best as she could. Though Mitch would eventually recover from the brush with Final Death, the pair learned a valuable lesson – the nature of their curse was different for each of them.\n\nThough initially Colleen attempted to nurture and care for her children, the Beast within her meant that her children would always be in danger so long as she and Mitch were part of their lives. After ten months of heartbreaking effort, Kady and Luke were remanded to the care of Colleen’s older sister, Meghan, under the cover that Colleen and Mitch were entering a long-term care facility for drug abuse. The shame of this abandonment would become so severe that Colleen could never bear to bring herself to see her family again.\n\nHowever, Mitch and Colleen soon found their own social group, as they formed a close bond with a band of local Kindred, all leaning upon one another for survival. Though her thin-blood nature makes her the most vulnerable member of her Coterie, it also makes her uniquely capable to handle daylight tasks. As a result, she has taken on the mantle of ‘provider,’ and spends most of her daytime solidarity hunting down the Coterie’s next bagged lunch.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v1jnNoiN4y0AOCH8hKRjNW9", "key": "Kindred Nights:", "name": "Kindred Nights:", "parent": "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v1o8up0P7FeaFN1g9sp28z3": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "You have managed to replicate the way in which the Wolves harvest vampiric body parts without them immediately decaying into dust. While you are certain to not gain the benefits they do by grafting such parts onto yourself, such a talent can nevertheless prove useful when it comes to preserving evidence, or grisly keepsakes. By dousing the organ or extremity into one Rouse Check’s worth of vitae and succeeding at a Resolve + Occult roll (diff. 3), the vampire may embalm the object for a year, at which time the preservation needs to be renewed. Final Death of the caster, however, immediately renders this preservation null.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v1o8up0P7FeaFN1g9sp28z3", "key": "Carrion Preservation", "name": "Carrion Preservation", "parent": "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 3, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#v1yYUsv376mLvdGqLd3ESdx": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Though the age of Prohibition and gangsters may be over, organized crime still finds a foothold in St. Paul. From Babyface Nelson, to John Dillinger, to Machine Gun Kelly, you represent a heritage of underworld culture that lives on to the modern nights. You gain a +2 dice bonus to all Streetwise rolls made to gather information on local criminal activity, and a specialty of your choice in Larceny.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v1yYUsv376mLvdGqLd3ESdx", "key": "Criminal History", "name": "Criminal History", "parent": "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 3, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#v2E5q9bGjiEZhACsWfskMvQ": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vQ05nvQOXUxzZBiC5iETKyw"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v2E5q9bGjiEZhACsWfskMvQ", "key": "Court of Samantha", "name": "Court of Samantha", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vAq7SfziwCcfkWORfVA4Pvu", "#vYY6HESkKvtokTz7jvWczwt", "#v1yYUsv376mLvdGqLd3ESdx", "#vPJ86DWzL9eyAgCcdTejXjX", "#vfWqHxS3BKWd33slWeeuxgp"], "choices": [], "desc": "Built upon native Dakota land, the kine have their various pseudonyms for it: Imnizaska, the Saintly City, the “Pig’s Eye,” and the Last City of the East. That final nickname is particularly true for the city’s Kindred, who view St. Paul as the last bastion of American Camarilla power before one reaches the lupine-dominated Rockies and the chaotic battlegrounds of the so-called Anarch Free States. Of late, even its sister city of Minneapolis has become more and more defiant of Camarilla authority. Nevertheless, those who claim praxis over St. Paul tend to claim the title happily: “Prince of the Twin Cities.”\n\nTo many within the Ivory Tower, St. Paul is little more than a bourgeois pretender; an up-jumped satellite domain to the realm of Chicago. But for those who have dwelled there through decades and centuries, St. Paul represents everything that Clan Toreador holds dear. From its Gallic origins, to the thriving (if humble) local arts scene, the Clan of the Rose fancy themselves as the bringers of culture and civilization to a raucous American frontier.\n\nFor the past century, the monarch of St. Paul has been Prince Samantha Merrain—a Toreador elder of seemingly ancient origins. Though her true age and generation are a closely guarded secret, Merrain has seemingly avoided the siren call of the Beckoning. A beloved protector of arts and culture to some—a spoiled, vapid tyrant to others—Merrain’s direct influence over Minneapolis has waxed and waned with the tenacity of the local Anarch movement, yet her hold over St. Paul is all but absolute.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV", "key": "St. Paul", "name": "St. Paul", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet", "typeHash": "#vtm5Loresheet0000001"}, "#v2Yjat7G0w5cdlV6qk94561": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Just because you’re paranoid doesn’t mean they’re not out to get you. You’ve managed to attract the attention of one of the Nictuku (or something that appears as one), and now it is but a matter of time before they catch up with you. You gain **Adversary** (••••); however, you may spend an equal number of points on haven merits relating to the added security measures taken against your phantom nemesis. Once per story, you may permanently sacrifice up to three dots in Backgrounds to make a clean getaway, at the Storyteller’s discretion.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v2Yjat7G0w5cdlV6qk94561", "key": "Deathmark", "name": "Deathmark", "parent": "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 4, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#v2tofC5zBQxh2vDa9OL5pEg": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v2tofC5zBQxh2vDa9OL5pEg", "key": "Kindred Relationships:", "name": "Kindred Relationships:", "parent": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "props": [{"items": [{"value": "**Elena Kowalski (Disdain)** “A useless sycophant who caters to both her own ego, and that of the Prince’s.”", "vk": "scalar"}, {"value": "**Jim Gershwin (Fool)** “There are few things more pathetic than an aged songbird desperately attempting to preen their molting plumage.”", "vk": "scalar"}, {"value": "**Mother Joe (Useful)** “A warrior, to be sure. But a blunt instrument. One that could possibly be wielded to greater effect.”", "vk": "scalar"}], "name": "Items", "of": "STRING", "vk": "list"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v45HAWhumPIUU7MgUxw68Yw": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "It was then that Singh was approached by that which he least expected and had never considered. A white man, in a poorly-fitting British officer’s uniform silently approached Singh’s dying body. Seeing him lash out like a cornered beast, the man revealed his true self -- a wandering Kindred named Sir Charles Stromwell. Stromwell gave Singh no choice as he hungrily supped at what little blood remained within his body, before forcing him to imbibe Stromwell’s own. As Singh was reborn, the two travelled the world by night, taking part in various conflicts as hired mercenaries, or simply unaffiliated interlopers. In the 1860s, the duo crossed the Atlantic where they revelled in the wanton bloodshed of the American Civil War. Eventually, the pair settled out West for a time, where Stromwell served as Primogen within the Twin Cities. Three years ago, Stromwell left the United States toward the conflict of the Gehenna Crusade. And while he did not feel the unshakeable, ancestral Beckoning, he was nevertheless summoned by the prospect of a great battle of immortals. Singh, having grown weary of his wanderlust, elected to remain behind, where he could hope to develop his own power not as Stromwell’s childe, but as a powerful Kindred in his own right.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v45HAWhumPIUU7MgUxw68Yw", "key": "Kindred Nights:", "name": "Kindred Nights:", "parent": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v5QQpLT11lrKBujAR0S4dPl": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "This unofficial district located in the northwest of the city is known among the local Kindred as the “Nod Lot.” Though the hunting there is just as bountiful as it is in more posh locales such as the Rack, the population of the Nod Lot consists of the discarded, forgotten, and despairing. You have cultivated a small Herd (••), whose blood resonance varies from the melancholic to completely absent. Add this to end: Additionally, feeding from such victims presents a high-risk of transferring blood-borne pathogens, potentially poisoning the well. You must take the Flaw Addiction (•) or Dark Secret - Plague Bearer (•).", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v5QQpLT11lrKBujAR0S4dPl", "key": "The Nod Lot", "name": "The Nod Lot", "parent": "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 1, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vTiC7GZvVXQHrkyWpMo3tOi", "#vdKtXkZP4GY4p9eirFvZJ5V", "#v1o8up0P7FeaFN1g9sp28z3", "#vMzDSL3OT3niTmwg6G4DBmO", "#vPnqOkEUldmQDRDSm6CibB0", "#vSKSYU9nqxt3OxwVsBXequJ"], "choices": [], "desc": "Discarded and disenfranchised ghouls forming themselves into confederations and cults is no new phenomenon. Animosity between servant and master is a tale as old as the practice of servitude itself, and woe to the vampire who carelessly abuses his faithful retainer. More than one city in the modern nights are plagued with bands of independent ghouls, stalking their former domitors to feast upon the vitae that fuels their unearthly addiction – using the gifts bestowed upon them to bite the hand that feeds.\n\nThough this practice is hardly novel, the cabal that calls itself the Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing has personalized this poetic justice in unique and perverse ways. The Wolves use their augmented blood coupled with a strange and blasphemous form of mortal Hedge Magic, to technomantically graft preserved kindred body-parts onto themselves. By harvesting, say, the eyes of a Kindred, they may, in turn, temporarily harness a semblance of that Kindred’s ability to control the minds of others through eye-contact, or to see into the depths of the soul.\n\nNo one truly knows from where these reprehensible mongrels first gained their taste of vitae, (though their passing familiarity with some form of necromancy implies a possible connection to a certain family of the Hecata) and any Kindred found responsible for such a blunder would surely find themselves upon the Red List. It is only their relatively small number and covert activities that keep them from being perceived as a bigger threat – instead, they are merely another faction of dangerous mortals to watch out for in the modern nights.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "key": "Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing", "name": "Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet", "typeHash": "#vtm5Loresheet0000001"}, "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#v1gEFg4SumJu8AfNJ7kBHgu", "#v1jnNoiN4y0AOCH8hKRjNW9", "#vPS8U3JGw8KmbYC9n5weQ6t", "#vxPJH4YO5DFO3kUF6cxnONm", "#vfY5xVTeH6fFXGtYq4E3KEB", "#vNrbaJmie8M6jwcLiGLKFeN", "#vt62dqijoo9elkeohhNSor9"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "key": "Colleen Pendergrass", "name": "Colleen Pendergrass", "parent": null, "props": [{"name": "Epitaph", "type": "STRING", "value": "Beleaguered Thin-Blood, Duskborn Den Mother", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Quote", "type": "STRING", "value": "“I’m exhausted... all of the time...”", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Clan", "type": "STRING", "value": "Thin-blood", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2, Charisma 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Secondary Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Health 5, Willpower 6", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Skills", "type": "STRING", "value": "Insight 2, Leadership 1, Persuasion 2, Subterfuge 2, Awareness 1, Finance 2, Medicine 2, Technology 2, Athletics 1, Craft (Domestic Crafts) 3, Drive 2, Larceny 2, Stealth 4, Survival 2, Animal Ken 2, Etiquette 3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Disciplines", "type": "STRING", "value": "None", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Thin-blood Merits", "type": "STRING", "value": "Day Drinker, Lifelike", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Thin-blood Flaws", "type": "STRING", "value": "Baby Teeth", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Sire", "type": "STRING", "value": "MITCH PENDERGRASS", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Embraced", "type": "STRING", "value": "2004", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Ambition", "type": "STRING", "value": "TO SEE HER CHILDREN, AGAIN.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Convictions", "type": "STRING", "value": "\"INNOCENTS SHOULD BE SHIELDED FROM HORROR.\" “ADAPT TO SURVIVE.\"", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Humanity", "type": "STRING", "value": "8", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Touchstones", "type": "STRING", "value": "KADY (20) AND LUKE (18), HER DAUGHTER AND SON.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Generation", "type": "STRING", "value": "14", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Blood Potency", "type": "STRING", "value": "0", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v7VLd6rypU1b84batrrw9qo": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vGkaApbX13DJZYiqLReB74g"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v7VLd6rypU1b84batrrw9qo", "key": "Plots and Schemes:", "name": "Plots and Schemes:", "parent": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "props": [{"name": "Endorse “The Next Big Thing”", "type": "STRING", "value": "Despite the unforgettable experience of the steam-carriage, Gershwin failed to capitalize on the opportunity, and dismissed it as merely an attraction -- had he known about the ubiquity of cars throughout the modern nights, he might have thought better of it. In Gershwin’s mind, were it not for his apathy, the name of Summer, Ogle & Co. might be as well known as the name Ford. Because of this perceived failure, Gershwin is obsessed with keeping an ear to the ground in the realm of bleeding-edge technology. In spite of this, Gershwin’s instincts are relatively poor, and he has passed over such opportunities as the radio, personal computer, and cellular phone, in favor of the carpet sweeper, 8-track, and 1-800 numbers.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v7eXeiyYtUzIZfkciESmX1J": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Elena was preserved not as a comely young maiden but as an accomplished grown woman. As such, though her face may be careworn and her skin not as supple as the convent girl she had been so many ages ago, she still carries herself with a poise and a dignity that is utterly majestic. **(Looks: Beautiful)**\n\nElena dresses herself in exquisite finery, though often it may seem slightly out-of-fashion. Exquisite furs and boas -- long opera gloves and strings of pearls -- Elena knows the value of a first impression and wishes for all who look upon her to recognize her wealth and privilege. She is not without her eccentricities, however, and recently has taken to keeping exotic pets. In recent nights, she does not travel to social occasions without her pet Fennec fox cradled within her arms.\n\nElena has acquired the services of the best identity launderers that money can buy and uses them to great effect. Throughout her long life, Elena has adopted many identities - “Helen Smith,” “Ellen Carmichael,” and even the subtle, yet slightly more Americanized “Elena Kowalski”.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v7eXeiyYtUzIZfkciESmX1J", "key": "Mask and Mien:", "name": "Mask and Mien:", "parent": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v7gLIU1NGdTMPybKqPMeKPG": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "While Elena may be a formidable undead monster, she prefers to keep her hands unsullied with the sordid acts that often come from the Eternal Struggle. As an unscrupulous member of the one percent, Elena has no qualms with hiring the services of disreputable firms such as that of Blackfire Security. While, for the most part, her small security detail is tasked with ensuring her personal safety, Blackfire contractors seldom ask too many questions when it comes to pre-emptive strikes. **(Allies 3)**", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v7gLIU1NGdTMPybKqPMeKPG", "key": "Blackfire Security", "name": "Blackfire Security", "parent": "#vRoYg3kGRu8HTmUf30fLlEB", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#v8m2hJt8CgdlHmbcdJAnQyB": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "More than one mysterious death or disappearance has been attributed, by conspiracy-minded Sewer Rats, to be the work of the dreaded Nictuku. Whether it’s a scouting party that has vanished beneath the streets of Manhattan, or a warren in St. Louis suddenly going dark, time and resources are often wasted on wild goose chases. Once per story, by examining the tell-tale signs (or lack thereof), you may definitively know whether such a crime was committed by your ancestral enemy, or some other circumstance.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v8m2hJt8CgdlHmbcdJAnQyB", "key": "Signal-to-noise", "name": "Signal-to-noise", "parent": "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 1, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#v90Lip3e5GbLG5sgyywEpEE": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Though the Discipline of Fortitude allows a Kindred to resist damage from bullets, blades, and even burning fire and sunlight. It does little, however, to keep the forces of physics at bay and an overwhelming blow can still stagger or knock prone the unprepared vampire. By shoring up their physical hardiness with vampiric **Potence**, the Kindred may maintain a steady footing when struck by a massive force.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#v90Lip3e5GbLG5sgyywEpEE", "key": "Obdurate", "name": "Obdurate", "parent": "#v1Bw5DQwhR49MbWP1oLpmXb", "props": [{"name": "Discipline", "type": "STRING", "value": "Fortitude", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Level", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 2, "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Amalgam", "type": "STRING", "value": "Potence 2", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Cost", "type": "STRING", "value": "One Rouse Check.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Dice Pools", "type": "STRING", "value": "Wits + Survival", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "System", "type": "STRING", "value": "When activated, a vampire may use this power to become a sturdy and strong immovable object. Vampires falling from great heights find themselves able to literally hit the ground running. Vampires struck by moving vehicles don’t budge an inch while the car crumples like aluminum. Users may consciously activate this ability in advance or may instinctively activate it by making a successful Stamina + Survival check at Difficulty 3. Any superficial damage received from falling or collisions is reduced by the user’s Fortitude score, before being halved.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Duration", "type": "STRING", "value": "One scene.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Discipline Power", "typeHash": "#vtm5DisciplinePower1"}, "#vA4kYnDgmhXwivshs9mwasY": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vA4kYnDgmhXwivshs9mwasY", "key": "Winter’s Teeth", "name": "Winter’s Teeth", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vAq7SfziwCcfkWORfVA4Pvu": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "If there is anything that Prince Samantha values, it’s talent. Those who are useful for furthering the Prince’s goals often find themselves awash in superficial praises from Merrain and her court. However, word travels fast between the Twin Cities, and those who may find themselves celebrated in St. Paul may be marked with suspicion elsewhere. You gain one rank (••) of Status (Camarilla) within the domain of St. Paul, however, you gain the Flaw Shunned (Anarchs) when in the borders of Minneapolis.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vAq7SfziwCcfkWORfVA4Pvu", "key": "Dirty Boot", "name": "Dirty Boot", "parent": "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 1, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vEKdg6JYh566yiFtPRan6iF", "#vl4dUHz7U21pTqcHeGaZzr1", "#v7VLd6rypU1b84batrrw9qo", "#vbbcDU7sTYOMG10E7gP5Kze", "#vSV0PuM4fd1ilqWuBqF8wv0", "#vWUFRFX8hBalPpNrS0yX42p", "#vjYGofXn0TNs19zvOIB9d6q", "#vlJEhBmht2313IWnSwUDLxA"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "key": "Jim Gershwin", "name": "Jim Gershwin", "parent": "#vYXxWahyNkObxzS0XivMeFh", "props": [{"name": "Epitaph", "type": "STRING", "value": "The Dilettante Poseur", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Quote", "type": "STRING", "value": "“They call it ‘Virtual Realism’. Possibly the most exciting thing since the kinetoscope!”", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Clan", "type": "STRING", "value": "Toreador", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2, Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3, Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Secondary Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Health 5, Willpower 6", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Skills", "type": "STRING", "value": "Athletics 2, Brawl 1, Craft 2 (Automotive Repair), Drive 3, Firearms 2, Animal Ken 1, Etiquette 3, Insight 2, Persuasion 3 (Pitching), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 3, Academics 3 (Research), Awareness 2, Finances 3, Investigation 2, Medicine 1, Occult 1, Science 2 (Engineering), Politics 3 (Camarilla), Technology 4", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Disciplines", "type": "STRING", "value": "Auspex 4, Celerity 2, Presence 3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Sire", "type": "STRING", "value": "HENRIETTA L’ABADIE", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Embraced", "type": "STRING", "value": "1833", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Ambition", "type": "STRING", "value": "TO SPONSOR AN ADVANCEMENT THAT WILL CHANGE THE WORLD.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Convictions", "type": "STRING", "value": "\"PROGRESS MUST NEVER BE STYMIED.\"", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Touchstones", "type": "STRING", "value": "GERSHWIN HAS GROWN FIXATED WITH BRITISH TECH MOGUL AND PHILANTHROPIST RICH LANCER, WHO MADE HIS FORTUNE OVERSEEING THE MUSIC LABEL COQUETTE RECORDS. JIM VIEWS LANCER’S PLAYBOY ATTITUDE AND \"TECH-BRO\" DEMEANOR AS SOMETHING WORTH ASPIRING TO AND FURTHER RESPECTS HIS SHREWD BUSINESS INSTINCTS.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Humanity", "type": "STRING", "value": "6", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Generation", "type": "STRING", "value": "10", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Blood Potency", "type": "STRING", "value": "2", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vBcxuCG6uZOu9dlmYkiUjsQ": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#v1Bw5DQwhR49MbWP1oLpmXb"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vBcxuCG6uZOu9dlmYkiUjsQ", "key": "Fortitude", "name": "Fortitude", "parent": "#vJIkg6w35VyWEHPFjBYdgJM", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vBoW9TlWxeCZIhtMRUfaYGn": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Primogen Calder Wendt (Confidant) Cecily likes that Calder never pretends to be anything more than what he is...a survivor who gets by because he’s charming and smart. She appreciates that he finds her past as an enemy of the Camarilla an asset. She favors clothing that appears soft and frivolous, masking her job as a physical enforcer.\n\nPrince Samantha Merrain (Respect) Cecily has seen the worst of Kindred kind but sees in Merrain someone who has genuine affection for her adopted home. She knows that Merrain is genuine, and that it’ll be her doom.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vBoW9TlWxeCZIhtMRUfaYGn", "key": "Kindred Relationships:", "name": "Kindred Relationships:", "parent": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vCBRTKNUf1R7ujklJkO9vJu": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Countess von Flemming still lives within the modern nights. She has nearly half-a-dozen childer to her name, all with the same training and tutelage as Elena. Is the venerable Ventrue perhaps setting her pawns, strategically, across the board?", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vCBRTKNUf1R7ujklJkO9vJu", "key": "Tool of Another", "name": "Tool of Another", "parent": "#vpqLjrnVVKdq5Ir1rXKofHG", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vCCeNFoVn0g5WyHyqpEVDlf": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "A favored power of the Roses, with this ability, the user may sublimate and infuse the powers of the blood into their works of art – capable of rendering sculptures so beautiful as to make the viewer fall in love with them, or paintings of such ghastly disquiet they make even the most visceral Caravaggio seem facile by comparison. This masterwork is merely an illusion, however -- a flash-in-the-pan beauty that does not withstand deep scrutiny.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vCCeNFoVn0g5WyHyqpEVDlf", "key": "Magnum Opus", "name": "Magnum Opus", "parent": "#vs9rCMBfBZXt6mzA15PYR7T", "props": [{"name": "Discipline", "type": "STRING", "value": "Presence", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Level", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 4, "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Amalgam", "type": "STRING", "value": "Auspex 3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Cost", "type": "STRING", "value": "One or more Rouse Checks.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Dice Pools", "type": "STRING", "value": "Charisma, Manipulation + Crafts", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "System", "type": "STRING", "value": "Before embarking on a **Project Roll** to create a work of art the user must make One Rouse Check for each roll made. The difficulty of the project must be 10 or higher. Upon successful completion of the project, the user finds that residual traces of their **Presence** linger within the work itself. When your artwork is on display, audiences must roll **Composure + Resolve** (Difficulty equal to the user’s Presence rank) or succumb to the rough equivalent of either **Awe** or **Daunt** exuding from the piece. A Critical Success on the resistance roll renders the subject immune to further influence by the piece. Note: By integrating Disciplines into its creation, the work of art has no true staying power, aside from the initial exposure. Critics and observers may find themselves suddenly able to critique flaws or imperfections once they have left the immediate area.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Duration", "type": "STRING", "value": "N/A", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Discipline Power", "typeHash": "#vtm5DisciplinePower1"}, "#vEKdg6JYh566yiFtPRan6iF": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "When James Gershwin was a young man, the world was in an unprecedented state of progress and innovation. As a child, he witnessed the proliferation of the steam locomotive, the exponential growth of factories, and the industrialization of civilization. As a young man, James (or “Jim,” to his friends) saw the future ahead of him and knew that there was no real limit to the possibilities of human ingenuity. Despite his fascination with engines and other such machinery, Jim had no education in engineering, and was a gentleman of leisure. He did, however, use his family’s riches to sponsor the efforts of actual inventors. Though most of the projects he supported were complete failures, Jim viewed his efforts as a labor of love rather than venture capitalism.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vEKdg6JYh566yiFtPRan6iF", "key": "Mortal Days:", "name": "Mortal Days:", "parent": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vEyCUsK8ii073J0x3x0v1X1": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Minneapolis, like many American cities, is plagued with a history of racism and societal injustice, whose wounds still bleed well into the modern nights. However, Minneapolis also has a strong tradition of those who fight for equal rights and representation. Perhaps you were once an active force for change within your community, or have otherwise become familiar to those who are, currently. You gain four dots to spend among Allies, Contacts, or Influence, to represent your affiliation with prominent grassroots movements, local leaders, or institutions. This activism among mortals has made you a target among your elite Camarilla enemies, however -- you must take the Flaw Status: Shunned - Camarilla (•).", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vEyCUsK8ii073J0x3x0v1X1", "key": "The Revolution", "name": "The Revolution", "parent": "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 3, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vFPXT21CvdCNSctbB3aO4Bu": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "As was ingrained in her from the moment of her Embrace, Elena has learned how to keep her true self buried deep, deep down. Elena is far from the shrinking violet she purports herself to be, and more than one of her victims have learned, first-hand, the true depths of her sadism. Such individuals do not often live to spread such rumors, however.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vFPXT21CvdCNSctbB3aO4Bu", "key": "Hints of Cruelty", "name": "Hints of Cruelty", "parent": "#vpqLjrnVVKdq5Ir1rXKofHG", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vGDuD8Ab2KFNggTl2qiSSxx": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Bosche Singh was born descended from a long line of Rajput — his family taking great pride in their warrior-caste. In the early 19th-Century, Bosche joined the Bengal Army, under the purview of the East India Trading Company. Though commanded by British officers, Singh was pleased to find that the majority of his comrades-in-arms were Rajput such as he, or Brahmin of high esteem. In 1839, Singh and his company were deployed to Kabul, taking part in the First Anglo-Afghan war. It was here, in the dusty mountains, that Singh took a grievous wound before his company was routed by an ambush from Afghan partisans. As he lay, bleeding out, he watched the sun set around him as twilight gave way to the dark of night. As the sleep of death threatened to overtake him, he raged against his imminent demise with a low and feral roar of fury.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vGDuD8Ab2KFNggTl2qiSSxx", "key": "Mortal Days:", "name": "Mortal Days:", "parent": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vGkaApbX13DJZYiqLReB74g": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Jim is displeased by the favor in which Tremere Primogen Calder Wendt has curried with Prince Samantha.\n\nHe believes that the Warlock’s intentions are impure, and that he is merely ingratiating himself to Merrain for the sole purpose of betraying her. In light of Prince Merrain’s death, Gershwin has begun to suspect that Wendt must have played some part in it, though he lacks the evidence to prove it. He seeks to leverage his position as Harpy (while it lasts) in order to irrevocably destroy Calder’s standing in the city.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vGkaApbX13DJZYiqLReB74g", "key": "Embarrass Calder Wendt", "name": "Embarrass Calder Wendt", "parent": "#v7VLd6rypU1b84batrrw9qo", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vQoctLznZ1CgXA33wAyhKVa", "#vffqoQ0VLoNvMTD0gtJW8TJ", "#vNX6OPhCZz1xRqNwU7dl6Hu", "#vVpGSdJlYNXhK1Pvg1oM0IQ", "#vO9uzKRBZ9fXYWRoncFKYkG", "#vBoW9TlWxeCZIhtMRUfaYGn", "#vxalXOW8Hgev8ex3EtWzp4i", "#vzx7tdtvFfwKflrnyyLfdQ1"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "key": "Cecily Bain", "name": "Cecily Bain", "parent": null, "props": [{"name": "Epitaph", "type": "STRING", "value": "Lone Wolf Without a Cub", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Quote", "type": "STRING", "value": "“We are the vampires of the Twin Cities...and we are desperately in need of some fucking public transportation.”", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Clan", "type": "STRING", "value": "Brujah", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4, Charisma 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 2, Intelligence 3, Wits 2, Resolve 4", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Secondary Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Health 9, Willpower 6", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Skills", "type": "STRING", "value": "Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Drive 3, Firearms 3, Larceny 1, Melee 3, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Intimidation 3, Leadership 2, Performance (Singing) 2, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 2, Academics 2, Awareness 3, Investigation 3, Occult 2, Politics 3, Technology 2", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Disciplines", "type": "STRING", "value": "Celerity 3, Dominate 1, Fortitude 2, Potence 3, Presence 2", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Sire", "type": "STRING", "value": "ASHA CHRISTESON", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Embraced", "type": "STRING", "value": "1979", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Ambition", "type": "STRING", "value": "TO SURVIVE. PREFERABLY ALONE.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Humanity", "type": "STRING", "value": "6", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Convictions", "type": "STRING", "value": "“SOME SECRETS ARE WORTH PROTECTING.\"", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Touchstones", "type": "STRING", "value": "CECILY REGULARLY VISITS HER SISTER, KAREN, WHO SUFFERS FROM DEMENTIA ASSOCIATED WITH ALZHEIMER’S.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Generation", "type": "STRING", "value": "11", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Blood Potency", "type": "STRING", "value": "3", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vJIkg6w35VyWEHPFjBYdgJM": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vV8aqiyZsPJp0CjPuzXyeDS", "#vfq5kx8XAA6T30OzNmU9l71", "#vBcxuCG6uZOu9dlmYkiUjsQ", "#viWfhIBT35Kq6oTNtoYpx31"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vJIkg6w35VyWEHPFjBYdgJM", "key": "New Powers", "name": "New Powers", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vKNYKphADCQUvlOD8mdcvET": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Elena and her (current) husband occupy a large and historic mansion in St. Paul’s Summit Avenue, located in the wealthy Macalester-Groveland neighborhood. Lightly armed security, electronic alarm systems, and closed-circuit surveillance allow Elena to relax within the safety of her haven with general peace of mind. **(Resources 4, Haven Rating: 2. Haven Merits: Location, Luxury, Security, Watchmen.)**", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vKNYKphADCQUvlOD8mdcvET", "key": "Domain and Haven:", "name": "Domain and Haven:", "parent": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vKkzz0XXNgApYgq7TNf7A65": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vKkzz0XXNgApYgq7TNf7A65", "key": "The Court of Prince Samantha (Part II)", "name": "The Court of Prince Samantha (Part II)", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vL4aYJEfEyT7dDMoBMJuG2E": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Jim looks to the future and the advancement of both human and vampire society. While his Victorian sentimentality is comfortable with a rigid social hierarchy, he also understands that he doesn’t have to be a weatherman to know which way the wind is blowing. It may take relatively little prodding in order to scoot Jim over the party-line.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vL4aYJEfEyT7dDMoBMJuG2E", "key": "Anarch Sympathies", "name": "Anarch Sympathies", "parent": "#vjYGofXn0TNs19zvOIB9d6q", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vM14JC58hmYRyYn2LiU7yXu": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Throughout the years, Elena has masqueraded as various scions of her own family -- using the mystique and the influence to infiltrate high-class social circles around the world. A brief marriage here, an inheritance there, and Elena has accrued such a vast amount of wealth that any deep scrutiny into her personal finances would reveal that she has not been vigilant about discretion. As the Second Inquisition nips at the heels of Kindred resources, such a flagrant money trail could spell her doom.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vM14JC58hmYRyYn2LiU7yXu", "key": "Messy Eater", "name": "Messy Eater", "parent": "#vpqLjrnVVKdq5Ir1rXKofHG", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vMzDSL3OT3niTmwg6G4DBmO": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "You have been victimized by the Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing, though have managed to escape. To this night, some up-jumped ghoul stalks the streets, wielding pieces of your body as their own. While this may serve them for now, you have managed to turn this plunder into a Trojan Horse. Once per Chronicle, you may attempt to inhabit the perception of your assailant, as per the Auspex power **Share the Senses** (**using Resolve + Insight.**) Should you already possess **Share the Senses**, you instead reduce the difficulty of the roll by two.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vMzDSL3OT3niTmwg6G4DBmO", "key": "A Wolf in the Fold", "name": "A Wolf in the Fold", "parent": "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 4, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vNX6OPhCZz1xRqNwU7dl6Hu": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Beholden to None: Cecily actively resists any and all offers to become an official part of the local Camarilla’s complicated ruling structure, instead demanding independence in return for her flawlessly executed services. (Status: Camarilla 3)", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vNX6OPhCZz1xRqNwU7dl6Hu", "key": "Plots and Schemes:", "name": "Plots and Schemes:", "parent": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vNYf0haVM2moNjIhtcyBwgr": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Patricide: Some doubt Singh’s tale of his sire’s venture to the Middle East. Many believe that the Great Tiger, hungry for power, committed diablerie on his creator.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vNYf0haVM2moNjIhtcyBwgr", "key": "Whispers:", "name": "Whispers:", "parent": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vNrbaJmie8M6jwcLiGLKFeN": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Untapped Potential. As a Thin-Blood, Colleen has exhibited no propensity at any particular discipline, nor is she versed in the practice of Duskborn alchemy. However, like many of the Thin-Bloods populating the Modern Nights, the only thing that can be expected of them is the unexpected.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vNrbaJmie8M6jwcLiGLKFeN", "key": "Whispers:", "name": "Whispers:", "parent": "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vNzQch3Hke5KJT6qrZ8WkPb": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "You have developed skills of survival and combat against more than just the Nictuku. Indeed, you have managed to hone yourself into a defensive weapon against any Kindred who would seek to consume the vitae within you. You gain the specialization **Brawl** (Kindred) and may add an additional +2 dice to all conflicted rolls against cannibalistic Kindred (diablerists, Blood Leeches, and the like.)", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vNzQch3Hke5KJT6qrZ8WkPb", "key": "Hunted-becomes-hunter", "name": "Hunted-becomes-hunter", "parent": "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 5, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vO9uzKRBZ9fXYWRoncFKYkG": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Street-Level Informants (Contacts 2) In conducting her work as protector of the Masquerade, Cecily often relies upon information provided by individuals savvy about the criminal underworld of the Twin Cities. If there’s a favored spot for dumping bodies, or fencing stolen goods, it’s a safe bet Cecily knows a guy who knows a guy.\n\nDwindling Goth Scene (Herd 1) Bela Lugosi may truly be dead; a far-cry from the Halcyon days of the late-80s/early-90s, the Goth-Punk subculture of the Twin Cities has considerably waned. To Cecily Bain, however, true taste is about quality, not quantity.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vO9uzKRBZ9fXYWRoncFKYkG", "key": "Thralls and Tools:", "name": "Thralls and Tools:", "parent": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vPJ86DWzL9eyAgCcdTejXjX": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Those who know how to cater to a Toreador Prince’s whims have learned to make themselves not only little worker bees, but beautiful social butterflies. You gain the specialty Etiquette (High Society) and may add +2 dice to any Social Conflict roll made within an Elysium or Courtly setting once per session.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vPJ86DWzL9eyAgCcdTejXjX", "key": "Courtier", "name": "Courtier", "parent": "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 4, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vPS8U3JGw8KmbYC9n5weQ6t": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "“On My Own.” Colleen and Mitch were on the fast track to divorce even before their respective Embraces, and, in her mind, has only been temporarily sidelined. The pair are in a mutually codependent relationship, but Colleen is constantly looking for the opportunity to make a clean break.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vPS8U3JGw8KmbYC9n5weQ6t", "key": "Plots and Schemes:", "name": "Plots and Schemes:", "parent": "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vPnqOkEUldmQDRDSm6CibB0": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "You have made yourself a mysterious benefactor to the Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing to such a degree that they have become your loyal, if ignorant, hounds. You gain Allies (••••) representing a cell of these redoubtable ghouls. Once per Chronicle, you may send this cell to dispatch a Kindred enemy. However, should the Wolves discover your true nature, said Allies may very easily become Enemies (••••) instead, not to mention any objections your local Camarilla may take to those who willingly aid and abet anathemas such as these.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vPnqOkEUldmQDRDSm6CibB0", "key": "The Shepherd", "name": "The Shepherd", "parent": "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 5, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vQ05nvQOXUxzZBiC5iETKyw": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "1 • BOSCHE SINGH\n\n2 • ELENA KOWALSKI\n\n3 • CORDELL BLOCK\n\n4 • PRINCE SAMANTHA MERRAIN\n\n5 • MOTHER JOE\n\n6 • CALDER WENDT\n\n7 • ERIN RUNNINGBEAR\n\nJIM GERSHWIN", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vQ05nvQOXUxzZBiC5iETKyw", "key": "Character Key (L to R)", "name": "Character Key (L to R)", "parent": "#v2E5q9bGjiEZhACsWfskMvQ", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vQoctLznZ1CgXA33wAyhKVa": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Cecily Bain was born Cecily Banashefski in 1952 in Pinewood, Minnesota, a small rural farming community outside Bemidji. When she was thirteen, her father was severely injured in a farming accident, and her uncle came to stay with the family to help run the farm. At seventeen, Cecily discovered her uncle had been abusing her eight-year-old sister, Karen, and told her mother, who, desperate not to disrupt the status quo, ignored the warnings. Cecily sought help from someone outside her household, making her way to the home of a neighbor rumored to be a witch. Instead, Cecily was introduced to her first Kindred, an Anarch woman who offered her the power to right wrongs herself.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vQoctLznZ1CgXA33wAyhKVa", "key": "Mortal Days:", "name": "Mortal Days:", "parent": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vR2UUAqmHrbfwLacXGAp3e7": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "While Minneapolis-St. Paul may not be the mecca for advancements in digital-space that Silicon Valley is, affordable housing and leasing has led many nascent tech companies to set up shop in the Twin Cities. Predictably, Jim Gershwin has ensured that many forward-thinking enterprises receive the funding necessary. **(Contacts 4, Influence 3)**", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vR2UUAqmHrbfwLacXGAp3e7", "key": "Start-Up Incubators", "name": "Start-Up Incubators", "parent": "#vSV0PuM4fd1ilqWuBqF8wv0", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vRoYg3kGRu8HTmUf30fLlEB": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#v7gLIU1NGdTMPybKqPMeKPG", "#vhh3CrnqCweL49eNYYe4dW8"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vRoYg3kGRu8HTmUf30fLlEB", "key": "Thralls and Tools:", "name": "Thralls and Tools:", "parent": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vSKSYU9nqxt3OxwVsBXequJ": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vSKSYU9nqxt3OxwVsBXequJ", "key": "Sample Wolf in Sheep’s Clothing (Deadly Mortal)", "name": "Sample Wolf in Sheep’s Clothing (Deadly Mortal)", "parent": "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "props": [{"name": "Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 4, Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3, Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 5.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Secondary Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Health 7, Willpower 8", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Skills", "type": "STRING", "value": "Academics 4, Awareness 3, Medicine 4, Occult (Hedge Magic) 5, Science 3, Technology 4, Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Craft 3, Drive 2, Firearms 2, Melee 2, Stealth 2, Insight 3, Intimidation 2.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Disciplines", "type": "STRING", "value": "Oblivion 1, Special*", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Special", "type": "STRING", "value": "In addition to the single Discipline power gained from being a ghoul, the Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing may have up to additional three dots in Disciplines, representing powers gained through grafting vampiric anatomy. Those powers must be chosen from the following: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude, Potence, Protean. (Note that these powers can exhibit a lot of variation from regular Disciplines, and the Storyteller is free to come up with new, unique, powers and variants.)", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Note", "type": "STRING", "value": "The Wolf may have up to three dots, spent however they please. Example: One Wolf may have Auspex 3, while another possesses Fortitude 2, Potence 1, and yet a third has Auspex 1, Dominate 1, Protean 1, etc.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vSV0PuM4fd1ilqWuBqF8wv0": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vR2UUAqmHrbfwLacXGAp3e7", "#vy7zD4GNWfTRCTZ1sceABwb"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vSV0PuM4fd1ilqWuBqF8wv0", "key": "Thralls and Tools:", "name": "Thralls and Tools:", "parent": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vTiC7GZvVXQHrkyWpMo3tOi": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "As their names suggest, the Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing are deadly simply because, as ghouled mortals, Kindred have a tendency to underestimate them – allowing them to get in close enough to strike with lethal precision. You have learned to recognize the tell-tale signs of these abominations as your Beast instinctively finds itself agitated around these callous usurpers.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vTiC7GZvVXQHrkyWpMo3tOi", "key": "What Big Teeth You Have!", "name": "What Big Teeth You Have!", "parent": "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 1, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vV8aqiyZsPJp0CjPuzXyeDS": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vu8iRHUbIE53tGnuWymPLuF"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vV8aqiyZsPJp0CjPuzXyeDS", "key": "Animalism", "name": "Animalism", "parent": "#vJIkg6w35VyWEHPFjBYdgJM", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vVpGSdJlYNXhK1Pvg1oM0IQ": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "In the late-90s, Cecily secured a warehouse space above the LOVELAND 24-hour sex shop, reasoning no one would question her coming and going at all hours, while occasionally providing a drunken snack showing up, confused, lost and horny on her doorstep. The neighborhood has gentrified around her and the shop, and she regularly wonders when Loveland will be replaced with a brewery or coffee shop. (Haven Rating: 2. Haven Merits: Location, Palisade)", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vVpGSdJlYNXhK1Pvg1oM0IQ", "key": "Domain and Haven:", "name": "Domain and Haven:", "parent": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vWUFRFX8hBalPpNrS0yX42p": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "**Bosche Singh (Blackguard)** \"A pugnacious pugilist without an ounce of subtlety! Still, I’d like to meet his tailor.\"\n\n**Elena Kowalski (Rakehell)** “Isn’t the Clan of Kings known for desiring thrones? Why waste immortality by simply existing?\"\n\n**Mother Joe (Mooncalf)** “The chap has a lethal uppercut, to be sure -- but I’m uncertain if he can lace his own boots.”", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vWUFRFX8hBalPpNrS0yX42p", "key": "Kindred Relationships:", "name": "Kindred Relationships:", "parent": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#v5QQpLT11lrKBujAR0S4dPl", "#vdtZlPSkYDGiq5Vz8oTYa2R", "#vEyCUsK8ii073J0x3x0v1X1", "#vpb4ZKCCKmMKSAb1poWvynJ", "#viK1fX42yoQH6APB1kEMVle"], "choices": [], "desc": "While St. Paul may claim the distinction of age over her twin sister city, Minneapolis has her beat on both size and population. Beginning life as a milling outpost along the Mississippi river, Minneapolis has swung back and forth on the pendulum of progress in nights since.\n\nSkyscrapers loom proudly over the downtown district while soft, yellow streetlights illuminate the fine dining of the riverfront. Between the city’s expansive sculpture garden and the Minneapolis Institute of Art, an appreciation for the fine arts has been blended into the city’s soul. Outside of New York City, Minneapolis boasts the largest number of theaters per capita in the United States. Even pop culture has been shaped by the City of Lakes, who can claim famed musicians such as Bob Dylan and Prince as native sons.\n\nWhen the Camarilla arrived in Minneapolis, they had already laid claim to the sister city of St. Paul. Despite Anarch protestations, Prince Samantha Merrain has claimed praxis over both of the Twin Cities and considers all Kindred dwelling within to be her subjects. However, cooler heads within the Camarilla of the domains are wary to directly support her reign, having grown fearful of uprisings in similarly fractured domains, such as Berlin. Some within the Anarch movement have also noticed certain similarities to those of their German brethren, and rumors of a possible revolt have begun to propagate the night...", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM", "key": "Minneapolis", "name": "Minneapolis", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet", "typeHash": "#vtm5Loresheet0000001"}, "#vXh1ch0ZWnwvLtQtYWyZQM5": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "**None.** Unlike a great many of the Kindred that surround her, Elena is quite content to simply live out her unlife in relative comfort and luxury. She wants for nothing, because she has it all. In Elena’s mind, it is no shame to serve rather than to rule, for heavy is the head that wears the crown.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vXh1ch0ZWnwvLtQtYWyZQM5", "key": "Plots and Schemes:", "name": "Plots and Schemes:", "parent": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vXolunYOWd2LBxkaeQiwz0W": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vXolunYOWd2LBxkaeQiwz0W", "key": "The Court of Prince Samantha (Part I)", "name": "The Court of Prince Samantha (Part I)", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vYXxWahyNkObxzS0XivMeFh": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vYXxWahyNkObxzS0XivMeFh", "key": "The Court of Prince Samantha (Part III)", "name": "The Court of Prince Samantha (Part III)", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vYY6HESkKvtokTz7jvWczwt": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "An open secret to locals, the man-made caves located underneath the otherwise innocuous Wabasha Street have played host to miners, mushroom farmers, bootleggers, and nightclubs throughout the years. Suffice it to say, their subterranean location has made them the ideal haven for Kindred, and many an Elysium has been held in the spacious, sandstone dancehall carved into the underground tunnels. As one of the denizens of the caves, you gain Haven (••) with the merits Postern (•) and Luxury (•).", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vYY6HESkKvtokTz7jvWczwt", "key": "The Caves", "name": "The Caves", "parent": "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 2, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vbViiiNkA7tGZqhk0Kuy4w8": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "“Darling James gets ever so passionate about such trivial things. It is quite precious to observe.\"", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vbViiiNkA7tGZqhk0Kuy4w8", "key": "Jim Gershwin (Plaything)", "name": "Jim Gershwin (Plaything)", "parent": "#vkxkw5qXOwxZUvd3LcckGsh", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vbbcDU7sTYOMG10E7gP5Kze": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "In 1977, Gershwin became the proprietor of a nightclub known as Disco USA. By 1982, it was completely remodeled and renamed Hank’s, reflecting a more Country-Western vibe. In 1997, Hank’s became Hankies, Minneapolis’ newest gay bar. By 2005, Hankies had reverted back to the now nostalgic Disco USA, until the novelty wore off and it was closed in 2007. After six years in reinventive torpor, the venue finally reopened as Rhapsody in Blue, a hipster cocktail and piano bar. Here, patrons may sip gin and tonics from mason jars at absurd mark-ups in exchange for chill vibes and an exclusive environment, uninviting to outsiders. Since the initial venue’s opening, Jim has directly overseen operations from his apartment, located upstairs. And while his pseudonym is no longer on the lease, not a single drink is poured behind the bar without Jim knowing about it. **(Haven Rating: 2, Haven Benefits: Location, Luxury, Postern, Security.)**\n\nGershwin’s feeding ground extends to the entirety of Northloop and the trendy Warehouse District of Minneapolis. Jim is not particularly draconian when it comes to hunting and feeding rights and tends to look the other way whenever a group of Anarchs wants to snack on a few bar-hoppers or sports fans -- provided that they don’t leave a mess. **(Herd 3, Resources 3)**", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vbbcDU7sTYOMG10E7gP5Kze", "key": "Domain and Haven:", "name": "Domain and Haven:", "parent": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vbxm6Cr5agSlJWHglIjnqwV": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "By subtly projecting their Beast into a mortal animal, the vampire may cause it to revert to its most base and primal of instincts. Loyal guard dogs suddenly become ravenous, slathering curs and prized thoroughbreds throw their riders as they champ and buck in mad panic.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vbxm6Cr5agSlJWHglIjnqwV", "key": "Atavism", "name": "Atavism", "parent": "#vu8iRHUbIE53tGnuWymPLuF", "props": [{"name": "Discipline", "type": "STRING", "value": "Animalism", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Level", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 2, "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Cost", "type": "STRING", "value": "One Rouse Check", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Dice Pools", "type": "STRING", "value": "Composure + Animalism", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "System", "type": "STRING", "value": "The target must be able to sense (smell, hear, or see) the user in question to use this power. Roll Composure + Animalism vs. Difficulty 1–4, depending on type of animal, its training, and whether or not it is a ghoul. A win against the target allows the user to choose one of two primal responses: Fight or Flight. If Fight is chosen, the creature reacts in kind, lashing out at the closest perceived threat or prey. If Flight, the creature instead flies into a panic, trying to escape its surroundings at any cost to their safety. Well-trained and faithful animals tend to shake off this reaction quickly, and so, clever users tend to time their uses of this power in order to create maximum effect.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Duration", "type": "STRING", "value": "A number of rounds equal to the test margin plus one, or the entire Scene in the case of a critical win.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Discipline Power", "typeHash": "#vtm5DisciplinePower1"}, "#vcdYIzP2CohDSis5knG1fBK": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Khan Ascendant: Bosche is uneasy with not being the top predator within his territory. While more than a match for most Kindred, when it comes to battles of claw and fang, Bosche lacks the critical influence required to not only claim praxis over a city, but to hold it. It is, however, something he is actively working toward changing.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vcdYIzP2CohDSis5knG1fBK", "key": "Plots and Schemes:", "name": "Plots and Schemes:", "parent": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vdIHqOv8rcwxESEqIYNs0XI": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "“You mean that great big brute with the slack jaw? What Kindred would waste their vitae making something like that immortal?\"", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vdIHqOv8rcwxESEqIYNs0XI", "key": "Mother Joe (Revulsion)", "name": "Mother Joe (Revulsion)", "parent": "#vkxkw5qXOwxZUvd3LcckGsh", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vdKtXkZP4GY4p9eirFvZJ5V": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "You have engaged in a deadly game of cat-and-mouse with the Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing for years. The lines between predator and prey have become blurred as you seek out these deadly foes while simultaneously ensuring your own safety during daylight hours. You gain an extra die to all **Investigation** rolls made to track down or investigate the Wolves in Sheep’s Clothing, in addition to gaining an extra die to all rolls made to act during the daytime.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vdKtXkZP4GY4p9eirFvZJ5V", "key": "Huntsman", "name": "Huntsman", "parent": "#v5hIxl5veWqsa0kG0mWZR6r", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 2, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vdm8af3gVlOLQT553ztd7Ne": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Singh dresses in bright and ostentatious pastels and colors. However, this display is not that of the strutting peacock, but rather the attention-grabbing coloration of a venomous creature: I’m here, and I’m dangerous. Take note of me. Beneath his clothing, Bosche’s torso bears strange, striated discolorations -- a lasting influence from the frenzying Beast within him. In dealing with mortals, primarily as a means of promoting fights (both of legal exhibitions and underground “street level” scuffles,) Bosche operates under a number of pseudonyms -- never sticking with one for a long enough time to create a true mask around it.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vdm8af3gVlOLQT553ztd7Ne", "key": "Mask and Mien:", "name": "Mask and Mien:", "parent": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vdtZlPSkYDGiq5Vz8oTYa2R": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "You are one of the lucky few who has managed to make a name for themselves within the music industry as a performing artist. Unfortunately, since your Embrace, your renown has become a double-edged sword, especially after the highly publicized reports of your death. You gain Fame (•••), however, must also take the flaw Mask (Known Corpse).", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vdtZlPSkYDGiq5Vz8oTYa2R", "key": "The Artist Formerly Known As...", "name": "The Artist Formerly Known As...", "parent": "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 2, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vfWqHxS3BKWd33slWeeuxgp": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Perhaps your service to Prince Merrain has been so subtle as to not attract the ire of your fellow Kindred across the river. Or, perhaps you’ve become so well-embedded as an Anarch within St. Paul that none would dare question your presence in either city. You gain a cover identity, in the form of Mask (••), for the purposes of undercover travelling within whichever Twin City you do not reside. That identity may also gain two ranks of Status with either the Camarilla (for St. Paul) or the Anarchs (for Minneapolis.) Once per story, any egregious breaking of the Masquerade (or that city’s Traditions) may be blamed upon that false identity (and, by extension, that Sect), leaving you to suffer little to no consequences. This is an ideal strategy for both infiltrators and Agents Provocateur within both sects.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vfWqHxS3BKWd33slWeeuxgp", "key": "Dual Citizenship", "name": "Dual Citizenship", "parent": "#v2LRwlTyNXQlMO3eBhVtfJV", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 5, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vfY5xVTeH6fFXGtYq4E3KEB": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Mitch Pendergrass (Contempt) Her Sire and her estranged husband. Colleen and Mitch spend as much time as possible apart from one another -- a remarkably easy task considering that Mitch spends the day in torpor while Colleen tends to her own solitary errands.\n\nPriscilla (Confidant) The coterie’s newest member, Priscilla, has brought a much-needed feminine presence to the gang of bloodsuckers. Priscilla, for her part, is more than eager to provide an ear for Colleen’s gripes, gushings and gossip.\n\nKing Rat (Charming) Perhaps it is King Rat’s smaller stature, or his loathsome appearance, but Colleen views the Nosferatu as a proxy for her own children. Though King is quite capable of taking care of himself, Colleen can usually be trusted to dote upon the young man with all of the fuss of an overbearing mother.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vfY5xVTeH6fFXGtYq4E3KEB", "key": "Kindred Relationships:", "name": "Kindred Relationships:", "parent": "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vffqoQ0VLoNvMTD0gtJW8TJ": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Upon her Embrace, Cecily killed her uncle and mother, and euthanized her suffering father. Her sister, unaware of what had transpired, joined Cecily in escaping to the Twin Cities. Cecily regularly used her ability to cloud minds to keep her sister unaware of reality, which she believes eventually contributed to her susceptibility to dementia. While Cecily and Karen spent most nights engulfed in the Minneapolis hardcore punk music scene, Cecily was also secretly feeding on its members. Cecily became affiliated with the Anarch movement of the Cities, and actively resisted the Camarilla’s attempt at urban domination, headed by Primogen Calder Wendt. Eventually though, Cecily saw the writing on the wall, and realizing she needed some kind of stability to aid her ailing sister, joined the Ivory Tower as one of Prince Samantha Merrain’s “dirty boot” enforcers.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vffqoQ0VLoNvMTD0gtJW8TJ", "key": "Kindred Nights:", "name": "Kindred Nights:", "parent": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vfq5kx8XAA6T30OzNmU9l71": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vvwP9EY5GrMIwfIGZKdHMTF"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vfq5kx8XAA6T30OzNmU9l71", "key": "Blood Sorcery", "name": "Blood Sorcery", "parent": "#vJIkg6w35VyWEHPFjBYdgJM", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vhOlj1u0WtH86G6ZPTlaaaF": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "“I see him at Elysium often enough, and I know we’ve been introduced. But for the life of me I can’t seem to put the name to the face...”", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vhOlj1u0WtH86G6ZPTlaaaF", "key": "Bosche Singh (Ignorance)", "name": "Bosche Singh (Ignorance)", "parent": "#vkxkw5qXOwxZUvd3LcckGsh", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vGDuD8Ab2KFNggTl2qiSSxx", "#v45HAWhumPIUU7MgUxw68Yw", "#vcdYIzP2CohDSis5knG1fBK", "#vjPtuaADCwb3yBxSa9cN3MH", "#vzhT3hu6efHWx0vzUj4dlQk", "#v2tofC5zBQxh2vDa9OL5pEg", "#vNYf0haVM2moNjIhtcyBwgr", "#vdm8af3gVlOLQT553ztd7Ne"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "key": "Bosche Singh", "name": "Bosche Singh", "parent": "#vXolunYOWd2LBxkaeQiwz0W", "props": [{"name": "Epitaph", "type": "STRING", "value": "The Great Tiger", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Quote", "type": "STRING", "value": "“It is only when we are battling for survival that we are truly alive.”", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Clan", "type": "STRING", "value": "Gangrel", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3, Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4, Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Secondary Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Health 8, Willpower 7", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Skills", "type": "STRING", "value": "Athletics 3, Brawl 4 (Grappling), Craft (Smithing) 2, Drive 1, Firearms 2, Melee 4, Stealth 4, Survival 3 (Find Shelter), Animal Ken 3 (Dressage), Etiquette 2, Insight 3, Intimidation 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2, Academics (Geography) 2, Awareness 4, Finances 2, Investigation 2, Politics 2, Technology 1", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Disciplines", "type": "STRING", "value": "Animalism 3, Protean 4, Fortitude 2, Celerity 1, Potence 1", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Sire", "type": "STRING", "value": "SIR CHARLES STROMWELL", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Embraced", "type": "STRING", "value": "1841", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Ambition", "type": "STRING", "value": "TO BECOME PRINCE OF THE TWIN CITIES.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Convictions", "type": "STRING", "value": "“ALL ARE WORTHY OF SURVIVAL, BUT ONLY THE STRONG MAY THRIVE.\"", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Touchstones", "type": "STRING", "value": "SINGH HAS TAKEN NOTE OF A YOUNG MMA FIGHTER, SANDY NGO, WHO EXHIBITS A TRUE WARRIOR SPIRIT. HE HAS BEGUN GROOMING HER FOR COMPETITION AND HAS NOT ENTIRELY RULED OUT THE POSSIBILITY OF THE EMBRACE.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Humanity", "type": "STRING", "value": "4", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Generation", "type": "STRING", "value": "8", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Blood Potency", "type": "STRING", "value": "3", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vhh3CrnqCweL49eNYYe4dW8": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Elena has ghouled many people over her long life, though few manage to remain in her service for long. Lately, Elena has conscripted the services of a middle-aged man whom she simply refers to as “Junior.” Silent, sturdy and secretive, Junior serves as Elena’s chauffeur, daytime courier, and all-around toadie. **(Retainer 2)**", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vhh3CrnqCweL49eNYYe4dW8", "key": "Junior", "name": "Junior", "parent": "#vRoYg3kGRu8HTmUf30fLlEB", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#viK1fX42yoQH6APB1kEMVle": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "In 2003, a riot stemming from a University of Minneapolis hockey victory was blamed on the Anarch community. Prince Merrain capitalized upon the opportunity to cripple Minneapolis’ Anarch leadership, and had three of the six perpetrators put to Final Death. The remaining three were forcibly blood bound to the Prince to ensure their continued loyalty. You are one of the surviving three. Your blood bond has broken, and now, you and your kin hunger for retribution. Once per chronicle, you may evoke the memory of the Minneapolis Six in order to sway the Anarch community to your cause, at the discretion of the Storyteller.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#viK1fX42yoQH6APB1kEMVle", "key": "The Minneapolis Six", "name": "The Minneapolis Six", "parent": "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 5, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#viWfhIBT35Kq6oTNtoYpx31": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vs9rCMBfBZXt6mzA15PYR7T"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#viWfhIBT35Kq6oTNtoYpx31", "key": "Presence", "name": "Presence", "parent": "#vJIkg6w35VyWEHPFjBYdgJM", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#viciuXx2u4U4nA21m322SkC": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Upon her Baptism into the night, Elena Kowalska was presented with an opportunity after the disastrous Napoleonic conflicts which tore Poland asunder. With her family having been utterly decimated and left without an heir, it was then that the prodigal “missing heiress” returned, filled with fanciful tales of an abduction and captivity by dreadful Russian agents, a daring escape, and a life spent in exile. So taken were the executors of the familial estate with the magnificent tale that they immediately took her at her word, and Elena soon found her family’s vast inheritance to be all hers. With a trove of gold and riches but no home to speak of, she took her vast fortune and set out for more hospitable climes.\n\nAcross the centuries Elena has put up her tent posts in various different cities and countries, having spent the last several decades within the American midwest as a darling of the Court of Prince Samantha Merrain.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#viciuXx2u4U4nA21m322SkC", "key": "Kindred Nights:", "name": "Kindred Nights:", "parent": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vjPtuaADCwb3yBxSa9cN3MH": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "In his effort to exert a wider control over his own niche of the city, Singh has taken to procuring a number of gymnasiums and sporting venues as both his personal hunting grounds and his havens. Singh’s Gangrel blood rebels at the idea of staying in one place for too long, and so varies his resting place, night after night. (Various level 1 Havens)", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vjPtuaADCwb3yBxSa9cN3MH", "key": "Domain and Haven:", "name": "Domain and Haven:", "parent": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vjYGofXn0TNs19zvOIB9d6q": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vza0P2iWVq8aUv9YhPMJmwc", "#vL4aYJEfEyT7dDMoBMJuG2E"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vjYGofXn0TNs19zvOIB9d6q", "key": "Whispers:", "name": "Whispers:", "parent": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "props": [{"name": "Taking to the Airwaves", "type": "STRING", "value": "For eight seasons, the reality-competition show Lion’s Den has broken network television ratings records. Centered around various entrepreneurs and inventors pitching their products to a panel of investors with the goal of receiving corporate backing. Rumor has it that Jim has been bankrolling production on this show in order to sift out the truly inspiring inventors from the talent pool before any of the panelists have a chance to partner with them.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vkxkw5qXOwxZUvd3LcckGsh": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vhOlj1u0WtH86G6ZPTlaaaF", "#vbViiiNkA7tGZqhk0Kuy4w8", "#vdIHqOv8rcwxESEqIYNs0XI"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vkxkw5qXOwxZUvd3LcckGsh", "key": "Kindred Relationships:", "name": "Kindred Relationships:", "parent": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vl4dUHz7U21pTqcHeGaZzr1": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "One evening, Gershwin attended an exhibition in Southampton, showcasing a marvelous new machine referred to as the “horseless steam carriage,” created by the shipwright firm, Summer, Ogle & Co. The showcase featured a twelve-passenger bus that ran on steam locomotion, not on an inlaid track, but on the same streets and roads as any other carriage. The northbound excursion from Southampton to London was proclaimed to last only five hours, beginning shortly after sundown, and was attended by numerous members of Europe’s futurist minds, including Charles Babbage. Also in attendance was the French Toreador socialite, Henrietta L’Abadie, who was utterly taken with Gershwin’s impassioned gesticulations and contagious anticipation for all things novel. As the carriage arrived in London, shortly before midnight, Henrietta invited James to her lodgings, where they spent the evening speaking, until the sun rose and both of them fell into slumber. For an entire week, James and Henrietta spent every moment in each other’s company, sharing in Gershwin’s predictions of the future and Henrietta’s eyewitness accounts of ages past. By the end of the week, Jim was pleading with Henrietta for the Embrace. No matter how dark the shadow of night, the brightness of the future would surely drown it out. Henrietta’s unbeating heart was moved, and so, obliged him.\n\nBut hope for the future ran out for Henrietta. At the turn of the twentieth century, humanity’s love of innovation and invention was harnessed for industrialized warfare, and her beloved France was ripped asunder. Leaving her Childe with a blood-tear stained letter, Henrietta walked into the sunrise. Devastated by the loss of his Sire, Gershwin followed his beloved’s letter, and sailed across the Atlantic in search of Samantha Merrain, a fellow rose named by Henrietta. “Proclaim yourself of my Blood, and Merrain shall know I’ve come to claim my boon.” Indeed, Merrain held true to whatever pact the two had made, and so she took Jim under her wing.\n\nSince then, Gershwin has acted as Prince Samantha’s Harpy -- ensuring that the record of prestation in Prince Samantha’s domain is well-documented, and that those of strong reputation are rewarded or rebuked, accordingly. He has also acted as the Prince’s link to the modern world -- a notion rather vexing to many Camarilla neonates and fledglings, as Gershwin’s own grasp on what is “new” or “relevant” is not always prescient.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vl4dUHz7U21pTqcHeGaZzr1", "key": "Kindred Nights:", "name": "Kindred Nights:", "parent": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vlJEhBmht2313IWnSwUDLxA": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Ever since his mortal life, Jim has always dressed himself with the latest fashion, constantly keeping up with the most relevant trends for young, attractive men. While always ensuring to dress within his age demographic, Jim also keeps his style in accordance with his own personality and temperament. Blending contemporary street-fashion with timeless aesthetics, Jim takes credit for bringing back vintage menswear. **(Looks: Beautiful)**\n\nWhen operating among mortal circles, Jim tends to prefer using proxies as opposed to dealing with individuals directly. As a young man who appears to be in his late twenties, he recognizes that, many times, the appearance of an aged, established man is more soothing to investors than upstart young entrepreneurs. Still, he does maintain several fake names and shell companies for the purposes of navigating mortal business affairs. **(Mask 2)**", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vlJEhBmht2313IWnSwUDLxA", "key": "Mask and Mien:", "name": "Mask and Mien:", "parent": "#vBNbiUNb2oQGNKWcwAZGAvH", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#v1QzV9xOVZp0nkqdKhWqalS", "#viciuXx2u4U4nA21m322SkC", "#vXh1ch0ZWnwvLtQtYWyZQM5", "#vKNYKphADCQUvlOD8mdcvET", "#vRoYg3kGRu8HTmUf30fLlEB", "#vkxkw5qXOwxZUvd3LcckGsh", "#vpqLjrnVVKdq5Ir1rXKofHG", "#v7eXeiyYtUzIZfkciESmX1J"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "key": "Elena Kowalski (Kowalska)", "name": "Elena Kowalski (Kowalska)", "parent": "#vKkzz0XXNgApYgq7TNf7A65", "props": [{"name": "Epitaph", "type": "STRING", "value": "The Long Con", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Quote", "type": "STRING", "value": "“The portrait? My great-grandmother. Why yes, the resemblance is striking!”", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Clan", "type": "STRING", "value": "Ventrue", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Sire", "type": "STRING", "value": "COUNTESS GRETEL VON FLEMMING", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Embraced", "type": "STRING", "value": "1796", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Ambition", "type": "STRING", "value": "TO LIVE FOREVER, IN STYLE.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Convictions", "type": "STRING", "value": "“NEVER LET ANYONE KNOW WHAT YOU’RE TRULY CAPABLE OF\"", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Touchstones", "type": "STRING", "value": "EUGENE RUTHERFORD LANG (67). THE CFO OF HERRICK’S FOODS, A NATIONAL GROCERY STORE CHAIN. EUGENE IS THE LATEST IN A LONG LINE OF UNWARY MORTALS WHOM ELENA HAS CLEAVED HERSELF UNTO FOR THE PURPOSES OF EXPANDING HER REVENUE.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Humanity", "type": "STRING", "value": "3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Generation", "type": "STRING", "value": "9", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Blood Potency", "type": "STRING", "value": "2", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Strength 1, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3, Charisma 4, Manipulation 4, Composure 5, Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Secondary Attributes", "type": "STRING", "value": "Health 6, Willpower 8", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Disciplines", "type": "STRING", "value": "Animalism 1, Dominate 3, Presence 3", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Skills", "type": "STRING", "value": "Craft (Needlework) 2, Drive 2, Larceny 1, Stealth 2, Animal Ken 2, Etiquette 5 (High Society), Insight 4, Leadership 3, Performance (Storytelling) 3, Persuasion 4, Subterfuge 4, Academics (Seminary) 3, Awareness 2, Finance 4, Technology 3", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vpb4ZKCCKmMKSAb1poWvynJ": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "The Kindred of Clan Nosferatu infest the city of Minneapolis from the sewers and the riverfront, to the dark corners of the skywalk and the ruins of ancient flour mills. While many object to their loathsome presence, few can deny the invaluable intel that information brokers within the Clan of the Hidden will provide for the right price. You have somehow managed to ingratiate yourself to this cabal of secret-seekers; you may distribute three dots between Contacts and Mawla (Nosferatu Mawla only), and, once per story, you may gain one valuable piece of information (at storyteller’s discretion) relevant to your characters Ambition.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vpb4ZKCCKmMKSAb1poWvynJ", "key": "The River Rats", "name": "The River Rats", "parent": "#vX7vUPtbtam2dHjI3qhjwxM", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 4, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vpqLjrnVVKdq5Ir1rXKofHG": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vFPXT21CvdCNSctbB3aO4Bu", "#vM14JC58hmYRyYn2LiU7yXu", "#vCBRTKNUf1R7ujklJkO9vJu"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vpqLjrnVVKdq5Ir1rXKofHG", "key": "Whispers:", "name": "Whispers:", "parent": "#vly000j9mCcfrEeAHacjMev", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vpuY9nECAu6Ivi7R6GO9E76": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Most Nosferatu believe the most powerful weapon in their arsenal is the Discipline of Obfuscate. However, while this may make them all but imperceptible to humans, Kindred and other supernatural beings have senses that extend beyond mortal means. In keeping with their name, the Hidden have had to hone their skills to counter not only the perceptive Tremere regent on whom they are spying, but also the unknown shadows that haunt their every step. Once per session, when contesting against a power such as **Sense the Unseen**, you may add two dice to your **Obfuscate** roll.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vpuY9nECAu6Ivi7R6GO9E76", "key": "Blindspot", "name": "Blindspot", "parent": "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 3, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vrEcN1GjLUhLomhwu3wcw4j": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Whether through legend, gossip, or indirect exposure, you have grown obsessed with the concept of these ancestral nemeses and have devoted your unlife to the study of the Nictuku. When making an **Occult** or **Investigation** roll regarding the Nictuku you may add +2 dice to the roll.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vrEcN1GjLUhLomhwu3wcw4j", "key": "Morbid Curiosity", "name": "Morbid Curiosity", "parent": "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ", "props": [{"name": "Rating", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 2, "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet Level", "typeHash": "#vtm5LoresheetLevel01"}, "#vs9rCMBfBZXt6mzA15PYR7T": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vCCeNFoVn0g5WyHyqpEVDlf"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vs9rCMBfBZXt6mzA15PYR7T", "key": "Level 4", "name": "Level 4", "parent": "#viWfhIBT35Kq6oTNtoYpx31", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vt62dqijoo9elkeohhNSor9": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Colleen Pendergrass still possesses all of her credentials from her lifetime and attempts to keep them active and up-to-date. Her haggard and exhausted appearance assists in selling the illusion of her being twenty years older than she’d otherwise appear.\n\nColleen is a slender woman of 5’6, who appears anywhere from her late twenties to her early forties. Bright, poker-straight red hair falls to her mid-back, and her pale green eyes compliment her equally pale, lightly freckled cheeks. Colleen has no real sense of style or fashion and can usually be found wearing what’s clean or available.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vt62dqijoo9elkeohhNSor9", "key": "Mask and Mien:", "name": "Mask and Mien:", "parent": "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vu8iRHUbIE53tGnuWymPLuF": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vbxm6Cr5agSlJWHglIjnqwV"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vu8iRHUbIE53tGnuWymPLuF", "key": "Level 2", "name": "Level 2", "parent": "#vV8aqiyZsPJp0CjPuzXyeDS", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vujvJ8ZOHj2jiE6khpo8N8M": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "A pathologist working for the Medical Examiner's office in downtown Minneapolis, Rafael DeLuna's personal mission of revenge against vampires eventually gave rise to a well equipped and connected network of hunters popular with local law enforcements and prepper communities, who all carry a mortician's hammer as a signature weapon and as an insignia.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vujvJ8ZOHj2jiE6khpo8N8M", "key": "The Mortician's Army", "name": "The Mortician's Army", "parent": null, "props": [{"name": "Source", "type": "STRING", "value": "Winter's Teeth, Issue 9, page 32", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Transcribed From", "type": "STRING", "value": "the Vampire: The Masquerade wiki's summary (vtm.paradoxwikis.com/Loresheets, CC BY-SA 3.0); the levels are in print only and are not transcribed", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet", "typeHash": "#vtm5Loresheet0000001"}, "#vvwP9EY5GrMIwfIGZKdHMTF": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#vyNBdJ8g21jjk8CaZqs5hRE"], "choices": [], "desc": null, "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vvwP9EY5GrMIwfIGZKdHMTF", "key": "Level 1", "name": "Level 1", "parent": "#vfq5kx8XAA6T30OzNmU9l71", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vxPJH4YO5DFO3kUF6cxnONm": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Colleen and her Coterie all spend their days in the home Mitch and Colleen bought for themselves as newlyweds. Though it has fallen into disrepair due to lack of consistent maintenance, the two-story house, which rests in the shadow of the Duluth Ore Docks, has plenty of space for the errant Kindred needing somewhere to lay their head.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vxPJH4YO5DFO3kUF6cxnONm", "key": "Domain and Haven:", "name": "Domain and Haven:", "parent": "#v6DeTHcURCA6BXT17cxSmd2", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vxalXOW8Hgev8ex3EtWzp4i": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Dangerous Liaisons: Nobody knows of Cecily’s sister, Karen. And Cecily aims to keep it that way. Regardless, rumors have begun to circulate about just who the enigmatic Cecily Bain might be visiting, night after night -- current consensus seems to speculate a favored Blood Doll.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vxalXOW8Hgev8ex3EtWzp4i", "key": "Whispers:", "name": "Whispers:", "parent": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vy7zD4GNWfTRCTZ1sceABwb": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "As Prince Samantha’s Harpy, Gershwin understands that there are any number of ambitious fledglings and neonates willing to serve as his catspaw if it means moving up the social ladder. **(Status: Camarilla 4, Mawla 2)**", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vy7zD4GNWfTRCTZ1sceABwb", "key": "Twin Cities Camarilla", "name": "Twin Cities Camarilla", "parent": "#vSV0PuM4fd1ilqWuBqF8wv0", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vyNBdJ8g21jjk8CaZqs5hRE": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Learned only by the most ostentatious of Tremere, this power is used to manipulate blood or vitae into finely crafted images – whether entertaining your fellows at Elysium with gaudy magician’s tricks or diverting flowing rivulets into painstakingly precise Hermetic sigils.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vyNBdJ8g21jjk8CaZqs5hRE", "key": "Shape the Sanguine Sacrament", "name": "Shape the Sanguine Sacrament", "parent": "#vvwP9EY5GrMIwfIGZKdHMTF", "props": [{"name": "Discipline", "type": "STRING", "value": "Blood Sorcery", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Level", "type": "INTEGER", "value": 1, "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Cost", "type": "STRING", "value": "Free (or One Rouse Check if using own Blood)", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Dice Pools", "type": "STRING", "value": "Manipulation + Blood Sorcery", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "System", "type": "STRING", "value": "Using a measure of blood or vampiric vitae, the user may channel their mastery of Blood Sorcery to influence the very essence of the blood itself, to obey the user’s whim. By making a successful Manipulation + Blood Sorcery roll, the user may craft the blood into any shape or image they desire. Complexity of the image varies by difficulty – a simple message of “Help!” or a basic polygonal shape may only be at Difficulty 2, while a lengthy diatribe or an intricate sculpture may be Difficulty 4 or higher. Failure on this roll means the blood fails to form the desired shape or does not respond at all – a Critical Success not only forms the desired image, but negates the need for any further rolls to change its shape for the duration of the scene.", "vk": "scalar"}, {"name": "Duration", "type": "STRING", "value": "For the remainder of the scene, unless dispelled by the user.", "vk": "scalar"}], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Discipline Power", "typeHash": "#vtm5DisciplinePower1"}, "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": ["#v8m2hJt8CgdlHmbcdJAnQyB", "#vrEcN1GjLUhLomhwu3wcw4j", "#vpuY9nECAu6Ivi7R6GO9E76", "#v2Yjat7G0w5cdlV6qk94561", "#vNzQch3Hke5KJT6qrZ8WkPb"], "choices": [], "desc": "(Nosferatu Characters Only)\n\nIn the underground tunnels of the Clan of the Hidden, there are whispered legends and cautionary tales shared among the Sewer Rats. Sires warn their childer of dangers lurking in the darkest corners of night, and of monstrosities that would chill the vitae of even the most hideous of horrors.\n\nNictuku.\n\nThat single word is enough to spread like wildfire throughout the ranks of the Nosferatu rumor mill, sending neonates and elders alike scuttling back to their warrens in paranoid dread. To some, they are believed to be the vengeful offspring of the clan progenitor – a vindictive and cannibalistic bloodline whose thirst can only be sated by the blood of the Antediluvian’s lesser childer. To others, it is the colorful sobriquet applied to those Nosferatu who have succumbed to their Beasts – a less existential, if similarly harrowing, threat – and now stalk the caverns and catacombs of the world, hunting their own kind. Even others maintain that it is a title taken by the eldest of the clan, merely another mask adopted to feed upon their own.\n\nWhatever the truth may be, no Kindred currently active in the modern nights knows for sure, and those who are unlucky enough to actually encounter one of the Nictuku are certain never to survive to tell about it. You, however, have managed to piece together key pieces of knowledge that may, one night, save your unlife.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vyzWfFfqDgk4I4ebAUMlmLJ", "key": "The Nictuku", "name": "The Nictuku", "parent": null, "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": "Loresheet", "typeHash": "#vtm5Loresheet0000001"}, "#vza0P2iWVq8aUv9YhPMJmwc": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "In flagrant defiance of the Camarilla’s recent eschewing of modern technology, as a means of avoiding detection from the Second Inquisition, Jim Gershwin still keeps a very active social media presence -- typically through dummy accounts and assorted false identities. However, as savvy as Jim purports himself to be, his sense of privacy extends only as far as the various settings on various websites. Any dedicated hacker would find it quite simple to discover his identity.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vza0P2iWVq8aUv9YhPMJmwc", "key": "Digital Footprint", "name": "Digital Footprint", "parent": "#vjYGofXn0TNs19zvOIB9d6q", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vzhT3hu6efHWx0vzUj4dlQk": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Combat Junkies: Bosche has no interest in those who attend his gym purely for exercise or “bettering themselves.” Those that catch his eye tend to be the ones who step into the octagon with the desire to cause pain and achieve victory. (Allies 2, Retainers 2)\n\nThe Menagerie: Bosche has managed to infiltrate the staff of the Minnesota Zoo, located in nearby Apple Valley to the south. There, Singh has managed to cultivate a small herd from the humble collective of Bengal tigers currently held in captivity. While not his preference, Singh believes that feeding from these beasts of his homeland fill him with a sort of shamanic power, transferring their essence unto him. (Herd 1)", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vzhT3hu6efHWx0vzUj4dlQk", "key": "Thralls and Tools:", "name": "Thralls and Tools:", "parent": "#vhbus2c2zGI8kYMYxYN1Uns", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}, "#vzx7tdtvFfwKflrnyyLfdQ1": {"aliases": null, "book": "winters-teeth", "children": [], "choices": [], "desc": "Cecily makes use of a number of aliases and identities whenever the situation calls for it. None of them are particularly ironclad, and their largely disposable nature means most will not hold up to high-level scrutiny. (Mask 1)\n\nCecily has purposely changed her clothing to reflect the urban chic of the Camarilla, abandoning her old punk costume with her Anarch affiliation. She knows that the Court will accept someone who dresses the part, no matter that Kindred’s history, because surface appearance is all most Camarilla Kindred are interested in.", "entries": [], "enum": null, "file": "vtm5e-0.5-winters-teeth-vol-1.ttrpg", "form": "DEF", "guidance": [], "id": "#vzx7tdtvFfwKflrnyyLfdQ1", "key": "Mask and Mien:", "name": "Mask and Mien:", "parent": "#vI2O6ZzFYFsBuOTjiHMpmRa", "props": [], "refs": [], "slot": null, "table": null, "type": null, "typeHash": null}}, "src": "data/winters-teeth.js"};var T=window.VTM5E=window.VTM5E||{books:{},entities:{},loaded:{}};
T.loaded[d.src]=true;T.books[d.book.id]=d.book;
for(var h in d.entities){T.entities[h]=d.entities[h];}})();
